# Settings and theming (expense-tracker-mobile)

## Settings-driven UI

- User preferences live in Redux `userSettings` and localStorage `expensio_user_settings`, merged in `useSettingsState` (`src/features/settings/hooks/useSettingsState.js`).
- Declarative UI schema: `src/features/settings/constants/settingsConfig.js` — sections, items, `stateKey`, `labelKey`, `featureFlagKey`, `dependsOn`.
- New settings rows: extend `SETTINGS_SECTIONS` and i18n keys; do not invent parallel `localStorage` keys for the same concerns.

## Theme and palette

- `ThemeProvider` (`src/app/providers/ThemeProvider.jsx`) applies `injectTheme` from `src/shared/utils/theme/themeInjector.js` and `applyUserSettingsEnhancements` for font, compact, motion, contrast, focus, screen reader.
- Use **semantic** classes and CSS variables: `bg-background`, `text-foreground`, `border-border`, `primary`, `muted`, `destructive`, chart vars `var(--chart-1)` … `var(--chart-10)`.
- `html` gets `dark` or `light` class; prefer tokens over ad-hoc `dark:` unless necessary.

## Masking

- `maskSensitiveData` in `useUserSettings().settings`.
- Money: `useMoneyFormatter().format` — never raw `toFixed` for sensitive amounts in UI.
- Text: `useSensitiveText` / `maskSensitiveText` from `src/shared/hooks/settings/`.
- Charts: `MaskedChartTooltipContent`, `MaskedAmount` in `src/shared/components/`.

## Density and motion

- `.compact` on root affects spacing via `--app-spacing`; avoid hard-coded large padding that ignores compact mode.
- Respect `.reduce-motion`, `.no-animations`, `.high-contrast`, `.enhanced-focus` applied by `applyUserSettingsEnhancements`.

## Accessibility

- Meaningful controls: `aria-label` where icon-only; form fields associated with `Label`.
- Settings toggles map to real behavior (screen reader, keyboard shortcuts, etc.).

## Feature gates

- Settings sections use `FeatureGate` with `section.featureFlagKey` — see `src/features/settings/pages/SettingsPage.jsx`.

